    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f8c37d9d71c790f57bbdb3d69bb43143f27118a839886dc1b846a518fd60e476",
      "text": "After breakfast at the hotel, transfer to the airport for your flight to Campo Grande. On arrival, continue to the Pantanal, where you'll stay at Pousada Aguape on a full-board basis.\n\nThe Pantanal is a vast wetland plain and one of the best places to watch wildlife on this route. The terrain is more open than the dense rainforest, so you can often see animals from the road or by the water. Caimans, capybaras, anteaters, toucans, jaguars and hundreds of bird species live among the tall grass, rivers and lakes.\n\nDuring the dry season, animals gather closer to water. You may spot coatis and macaws along dirt roads. The programme includes walks, drives across the plains and horseback rides through wet stretches of savanna. In the evening, birds, frogs and insects are particularly easy to hear.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw62hj6e-l11w8-amanda",
        "model": "ChatGPT",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "Word Day 8 verifies the flight, transfers, lodge and excursions, but the site block adds specific wildlife, dry-season behaviour and evening sounds absent from those Word paragraphs. There is no complete matching Word passage."
      }
    },
